  "instance_name": "captive_chicken_stereotype",
  "label": "Captive Chicken Stereotype",
  "description": "The phrase 'held in captivity' refers to the stereotype of chickens as domesticated animals that are confined and controlled by humans. This stereotype is used in the meme to imply that women are similarly confined and controlled, reinforcing the idea that they are property to be managed and ultimately disposed of. This is a form of dehumanization that equates women with livestock.",
